  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An aqueous solution is prepared by dissolving <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;mole of an ionic salt in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> of water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The salt remains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math> dissociated in the solution. The vapour pressure of the solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>59</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>724</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hg</mi></math>. Vapor pressure of water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hg</mi></math>. The number of ions present per formula unit of the ionic salt is _____.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Number of ions present per formula unit of ionic salt <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p>Van &#39;t Hoff factor</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math></p><p>(Assuming <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math> dissociation)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Relative lowering in vapour pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>&#215;</mo></math> Mole fraction of solute</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>59</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>724</mn></mrow><mn>60</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1800</mn><mn>18</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0046</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0046</mn><mo>&#8776;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
